    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you use the quote form on this website we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name</li>
      <li>your phone number</li>
      <li>your email address</li>
      <li>your company name, if you provide one</li>
      <li>the suburb or site address, property type, service required, approximate
        size, timing and working-hours preferences you select</li>
      <li>the description you write in the message box</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you send photos by email rather than through the form, we also hold
      those images and they are treated the same way.
    </p>
    <p>We also record basic, aggregated, anonymous website usage statistics so we
      can see which pages are useful. We do not collect anything that identifies
      you personally through that.</p>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>
      So we can contact you about your enquiry, inspect the site, and prepare and
      send you a written quote. That is the entire purpose. We will not add you
      to a marketing list because you asked for a quote, and we will not pass
      your details to anyone else for marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else receives it</h2>
    <p>
      Our website is hosted on GitHub, and form submissions are delivered using a
      third-party form service. The information you type into the quote form is
      transmitted over an encrypted connection to
      <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, which forwards it to our email inbox.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell your information, and we do not disclose it to third parties
      except where the law requires it. If we ever need to pass site access or
      project information to a subcontractor to complete your job, we will tell
      you first.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries that do not become projects are deleted within
      <span class="ph">[PLACEHOLDER: e.g. 12]</span> months. Enquiries that do
      become projects are kept for as long as the contract requires and for the
      period afterwards in which we may need to deal with a warranty claim under
      our five-year coating warranty.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or
      cross-site tracking. You will not be asked to accept a cookie banner
      because there is nothing to accept.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two things do set small technical files: a spam-protection check when you
      submit the form, and standard server logs. Neither is used to track you
      across other websites.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the Australian Privacy Act 1988 you can ask us to tell you what
      personal information we hold about you, correct it if it is wrong, or
      delete it where we are not required to keep it. We will respond within a
      reasonable time and we will not charge you for it.
    </p>
    <p>
      To make a request, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      This website is served over encrypted HTTPS. The form you use is sent
      over an encrypted connection. No system is perfectly secure, but we do not
      collect anything from you that we do not need in order to quote for and
      complete your work.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes we will update the date at the top of this page.
      Questions about any of it are welcome — ask us.
    </p>
    <div class="notice" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
